In this folder, character modifiers are defined

The modifers are on the format:

modifer_key = {
	icon = icon_name
	
	# ( optional ) If yes, every application of this modifier as a timed modifier is kept as a separate instance
	# (removal removes the one expiring soonest). If no, re-adding it only extends the existing instance's
	# expiration date if the new one is later. Default: no
	stacking = no

	# ( optional ) If yes, the modifier's effects are not listed in its description
	# (only the '<modifier_key>_desc' loc, if it exists, is shown). Default: no
	hide_effects = no
	
	# Effects, such as
	# tax_mult = 0.25
	# county_opinion_add = -30

	# Modifier can have scale that'll be calculated once when effect assigns a modifier, and later
	# remains unchanged for the entire modifier duration
	# Can also be written as just 'scale = scale_scripted_value'
	scale = {

		# Scripted value - can be named value or direct math here
		# Evaluated with the scopes of the effect that assigns the modifier: this scope is the object that's
		# going to get the modifier; root and saved scopes are those of the calling effect
		# Scripted value top level description will be added to modifier description
		value = scale_scripted_value

		# Loc key that's used for base level entry, to show alongside with the scaled value
		desc = base_value_description

		# ( optional ) How modifier values are displayed. Default: default
		#   default  - scaled values if the scale is not 1, otherwise unscaled
		#   scaled   - always show scaled values
		#   unscaled - always show unscaled values
		display_mode = default/scaled/unscaled
	}
}

"modifier_key" is the name of the modifier, that is used in effects to apply it
"icon" decides which modifier icon to use. if it ends in positive or negative, the name of the modifier will be colored appropriately

